        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The Horizon T101, now the <strong class="text-white">T101 Connect</strong>, is a coherent
            walking treadmill: a 20 by 55-inch deck, 10% incline, a 300 lb rating, a console that needs
            no subscription and lifetime frame and motor cover. It was sold out at Horizon on 14 October
            2026, Horizon no longer publishes its motor rating, and it is not a running machine.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Owners should get the manual for their exact version from Horizon’s help centre, and anyone
            with a T101-05 should check for a TM734 or TM486 serial and the recall software. Runners
            should look at the 60-inch Horizons in our
            <a href="/best-horizon-treadmills/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">Horizon roundup</a>,
